{"name":"Quiver Tan","hex":"#8e7f6a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"quiver","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A container for arrows, crossbow bolts or darts, such as those fired from a bow, crossbow or blowgun.","A ready storage location for figurative tools or weapons."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Nimble, active."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quiver"},{"term":"tan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["The trigonometric function tangent."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tangale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Quiver","blocks":[{"text":"A quiver is a container for holding arrows or bolts. It can be carried on an archer's body, the bow, or the ground, depending on the type of shooting and the archer's personal preference. Quivers were traditionally made of leather, wood, furs, and other natural materials, but are now often made of metal or plastic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Wenceslas_Hollar_-_Quivers_and_hunting_horns.jpg/330px-Wenceslas_Hollar_-_Quivers_and_hunting_horns.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quiver"},{"title":"Tan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Tan is a pale tone of brown. The name is derived from tannum used in the tanning of leather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg/330px-Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tan_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Bayeux_Tapestry_scene51_Battle_of_Hastings_Norman_knights_and_archers.jpg/500px-Bayeux_Tapestry_scene51_Battle_of_Hastings_Norman_knights_and_archers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thum